Graph Cycle Detector
====================

Write a function:

    def graph_cycle_detector(graph: dict[int, list[int]]) -> bool

graph maps each node to the list of nodes it points to (a directed graph;
a node may point to nodes that have no key of their own). Return True if
the graph contains a cycle, False otherwise. Use DFS with a "currently in
the recursion path" set: seeing a node that is already on the current path
means a cycle. An empty graph has no cycle.

Examples:
    graph_cycle_detector({0: [1], 1: [2], 2: [0]}) -> True
    graph_cycle_detector({0: [1], 1: [2], 2: []}) -> False
    graph_cycle_detector({0: [0]}) -> True
    graph_cycle_detector({0: [1], 1: [], 2: [3], 3: [2]}) -> True
    graph_cycle_detector({0: [1, 2], 1: [3], 2: [3], 3: []}) -> False
    graph_cycle_detector({}) -> False
